  "command": "source 'scripts/env.sh' && CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_COMPOSER='/usr/bin/composer' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_WASM_MAX_LOAD='8' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_WASM_MODES='result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_WASM_OUTPUT='build/nominal-primitive-subtype-php-wasm-promotion/reviewed-result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_WASM_ROUTES='reviewed' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_WASM_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_PHP_WASM_HOST='build/php-wasm-host' LEAN_BRIDGE_TEST_PHP_COPIED_RUNTIME='build/nominal-primitive-subtype-php-wasm-input/php-wasm-runtime' LEAN_BRIDGE_PHP='/usr/bin/php' LEAN_WASM_ARTIFACT_TARGET='php-wasm-emscripten-3.1.68' LEAN_WASM_EMSDK='.toolchains/emsdk-php-wasm' LEAN_WASM_RUNTIME_PROFILE='browser' LEAN_WASM_RUNTIME_VARIANT='php-wasm-3.1.68' EMCC_CORES='2' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' 'node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' '--test-name-pattern=^installed primitive-base nominal PHP-Wasm packages reproduce and relocate reviewed result-only$' 'tests/helpers/nominal-primitive-subtype-php-wasm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Composer API, npm component and npm shared-runtime archives. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation; unchanged weak and strict callers replay in twelve Node and Chromium contexts after moving the installed tree. The standalone result-only API projects all nineteen primitive payloads through scalars, copied containers, records, variants and aliases without any input constructor selections. Primitive-base nominal PHP-Wasm acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, nested Pair/Array/Option/Except values, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce the complete Composer API, npm component and npm shared-runtime archives from two author roots, remove author and build roots, install offline, and replay twelve Node and Chromium contexts per selection twice after relocation. Those contexts cover embedded and Composer Node installations and Chromium bundles with startup/lazy loading and weak/strict callers on wasm32 PHP 8.4.1, Node 22.23.2 and Chromium 152.0.7977.75. The runs use 32-bit machine words, a 2 GiB free/available-memory floor and an 8.0 host-load admission ceiling. Original packages, receipts, caller/compiler records, executions and selected sources are retained; external toolchain and browser binaries are represented by identity rather than copied. PHP consumer source remains required at runtime. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent, dispatch-counted and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. Hosted current-revision acceptance remains assigned to the recurring workflow; archived absolute paths describe the original local runs and are not CI prerequisites.",
